      "q": "7. Deciding where to go for picnic.\nSuggestion\n(vii) We\ncan\ngo to any park nearby for picnic.\nExplanation:\nMay \u2013 used to give permission.\nMust \u2013 expresses obligation or something that is required.\nShould \u2013 used to offer advice or make a recommendation.\nMay \u2013 can also indicate a strong possibility.\nWould \u2013 commonly used to make polite requests.\nOught to \u2013 used to give strong advice or express what is the right thing to do.\nCan \u2013 used to show ability.\nThree Days to See Question Answer Class 7 \u2013 Let us listen (Page 36)\nYou will listen to a conversation between a mother and son. As you listen, select four true statements from 1-7 given below. (Transcript for the teacher on NCERT textbook page. 41)\ntable-3",
      "a": "wer:\nTrue \u2013 Reason: Anuj wants to understand what a screen reader is and how it helps blind people.\nFalse \u2013 Reason: Anuj\u2019s mother is confident that the school has facilities to support visually impaired students.\nTrue \u2013 Reason: Anuj says that Digital India is about becoming computer literate.\nTrue \u2013 Reason: Anuj\u2019s mother explains to him what assistive technologies are.\nFalse \u2013 Reason: Anuj did not know that visually impaired individuals can use computers until his mother told him.\nFalse \u2013 Reason: It is Anuj\u2019s mother who explains assistive technologies when he asks about Digital India.\nTrue \u2013 Reason: The mother believes that computers can greatly improve the quality of life for visually impaired people.\nClass 7 English Chapter 3 Question Answer \u2013 Let us Speak (Pages 36-37)\nWork in pairs. Take turns to speak for a minute on any one of the senses you value the most.\nUse the given prompts to frame your response before you speak.\nI value my sense of sight/sound/ touch/smell/taste the most because\u2026\nOne of my favourite experiences is\u2026\nThis is so because\u2026\nI appreciate being able to see/hear/ touch / smell / taste\u2026\nGod forbid, if I were to lose the sense of sight/sound/touch/smell/taste, it would make me feel\u2026\nI would not be able to\u2026\nI thank God that I am able to see/ hear / touch / smell / taste.\nRemember to\nspeak clearly and confidently\nglance at your notes for reference rather than reading\nmake eye contact\nuse gestures if you wish to\npronounce words clearly and avoid mumbling\nspeak at a steady, moderate pace\nAnswer:\nI value my sense of sight the most because it lets me experience the beauty of the world\u2014the vibrant colours of flowers, the sparkle of sunlight on water, and the warm smiles of the people I love. One of my favourite moments is watching the sunrise from a hilltop, when the sky transforms into shades of orange, pink, and gold, filling me with peace and hope. I also cherish seeing the faces of my family and friends, as their expressions reveal their feelings without a single word.\nIf I were ever to lose my sight, I would feel frightened and limited because I would no longer be able to enjoy books, paintings, or the wonders of nature. I would struggle to see my surroundings and would have to depend more on my other senses.\nI am truly grateful to God for my ability to see the beautiful things life offers, and I treasure every moment that my eyes allow me to experience the world.\nNCERT Class 7 English Poorvi Chapter 3 Question Answer \u2013 Let us write (Page 37)\nA descriptive paragraph describes a person, place, object or event to create a memorable experience for the reader. Write a descriptive paragraph describing a place that you visited recently.\nFollow the guidelines given below to draft this paragraph."
