      "q": "1. Rani-ki-Vav (the Queen\u2019s Stepwell) is located at Patan, Gujarat and is also on the World Heritage list by UNESCO. Stepwells are a distinctive form of water resource and storage systems on the Indian subcontinent, and were constructed during ancient times. They evolved over time from what was basically a pit in sandy soil towards elaborate multi-storey works of art and architecture.\nRani-ki-Vav\nSource: UNESCO\nNow, find out about the unique places in your village, region or state and share the details with your classmates and the teacher.",
