      "q": "4. Sports Camp Organiser: Explain\nhow you ensure safety and why you believe sports are beneficial for participants.\nPrompts\nIn my opinion\u2026\nFrom my point of view\u2026\nOne reason for this is\u2026\nI disagree with the notion that\u2026\nI support this perspective because\u2026\nI find it hard to agree because \u2026\nI believe that\u2026\nI disagree with\u2026\nI agree with the idea that..\nVocabulary you may use\nprecautions unique experiences fun safe enjoyable thrilling builds confidence concern explore overcome fear participate",
      "a": "wer:\nSchool student: I feel Physical Education should be a part of school activities because it keeps students healthy and boosts their confidence. It also adds excitement to the school routine and helps us learn to work together as a team.\nParent: I think Physical Education is important for children since it helps them discover their strengths and build courage. That said, safety must be a priority, so schools should follow proper guidelines and precautions.\nPhysical Education Teacher: I strongly believe Physical Education plays a key role in a child\u2019s overall development. It strengthens both body and mind, and sports naturally develop discipline, teamwork, and responsibility.\nSports camp organiser: I support the idea of sports and adventure activities because they are enjoyable and motivating when conducted responsibly. I focus on safety by providing training, using the right equipment, and ensuring all precautions are followed before the activities begin.\nNCERT Class 7 English Poorvi Chapter 12 Question Answer \u2013 Let us write (Pages 174-175)\nRead the various components of a formal letter from the box given below.\u2019\nNo.\nItems\n1\ncomplimentary close\n2\nreceiver\u2019s address\n3\nsubject\n4\ndate\n5\nintroduction\n6\nstatement of request\n7\nexpression of interest\n8\nsalutation\n9\nsignature line\n10\nsender\u2019s address\nQuestion 1. Now, read the letter given below and write the matching components.\nAnswer:\nSender\u2019s Address \u2192 Sender\u2019s address\nDate \u2192 Date\nReceiver\u2019s Address \u2192 Receiver\u2019s address\nSchool\nSubject: Request to join Adventure Club \u2192 Subject\nMadam/Sir, \u2192 Salutation\nI am Sreelakshmi, a student of Grade 7-C. I am interested 1 in adventure activities like trekking, hiking, rope climbing, and exploring sites of natural beauty. \u2192 Introduction\nI would love to be a part of the Adventure Club of the school and participate in the adventure activities organised. \u2192 Statement of request\nI request you to grant me permission to join the club. \u2192 Expression of interest\nYours sincerely, \u2192 Complimentary close\nSreelakshmi \u2192 Signature line\nQuestion 2. Write a letter to the Principal of your school requesting her to organise an excursion to a nearby hill station for Grade 7 students of your school.\nAnswer:\nRosebud International School\nDwarka, Delhi\n15th September, 2025\nTo\nThe Principal\nRosebud International School\nDwarka, Delhi\nSubject: Request for an excursion to a nearby hill station for Grade 7 students\nRespected Madam,\nI am writing on behalf of the students of Grade 7 to request permission to organise an excursion to a nearby hill station. We believe such a trip would be a wonderful learning experience as well as a refreshing break. It would give students the opportunity to connect with nature, understand the environment better, and take part in healthy outdoor activities.\nAn excursion like this can also help students develop teamwork, confidence, and a sense of responsibility outside the classroom setting. We assure you that we will strictly follow all school rules, safety instructions, and necessary guidelines during the journey and throughout the trip.\nWe kindly request you to consider our proposal and approve this excursion. We would be grateful if the school could arrange appropriate transport and ensure proper supervision for the students.\nWe look forward to your favourable response.\nThanking you\nYours sincerely\nSonal Mishra\nClass 7 A\nClass 7th English Chapter 12 Conquering the Summit Question Answer \u2013 Let us explore (Page 175)\nI. Find out more information about the following adventure sports in our country and complete the table given below:\nName\nArea\nPreferred Time of the Year\nEquipment Required\nSnow skiing\nSnow-covered hills\nSkis, ski suit, helmet, goggles, gloves\nTrekking\nHills\nSpring, Autumn, Winter\nPole, ropes, trekking shoes, hammer\nCamping\nGrassy areas\nAll year round\nTent, torch, water, food\nRiver Rafting\nAll year round\nScuba Diving\nSea\nScuba suit, mask, fins,\nsnorkel\nAnswer:\nName\nArea\nPreferred Time of the Year\nEquipment Required\nSnow skiing\nSnow-covered hills\nWinters\nSkis, ski suit, helmet, goggles, gloves\nTrekking\nHills\nSpring, Autumn, Winter\nPole, ropes, trekking shoes, hammer\nCamping\nGrassy areas\nAll year round\nTent, torch, water, food\nRiver Rafting\nDown flowing River\nAll year round\nHelmet, life jacket\nScuba Diving\nSea\nAll year round\nScuba suit, mask, fins,\nsnorkel\nII. Prepare an information booklet with fact sheets of five Indian mountaineers. Include the following information in the fact sheet."
