      "q": "5. The Portuguese attacked Ullal in response to Rani Abbakka\u2019s defiance.\n(v) Rani Abbakka in turn attacked the Portuguese Fort.\nClass 7 English Rani Abbakka Question Answer \u2013 Let us think and reflect (Pages 214-215)\nI. Read the extract given below and answer the questions that follow.\nPortuguese envoy: Our Governor has sent me to remind you that the annual tribute from Ullal is long overdue and\u2026\nRani Abbakka: We are a sovereign country. We don\u2019t pay tribute to Portugal. And we don\u2019t take orders from the Portuguese!\nPortuguese envoy: Your Majesty, you will regret your stand.\nAbbakka ordered merchant ships to be built and in alliance with the Zamorin of Kozhikode, she defied the Portuguese and established a hugely profitable trading relation with Arabia.\nQuestion 1. What does the word \u2018tribute\u2019 mean in this context?",
      "a": "wer:\nIn this context, \u2018tribute\u2019 means a payment that the Portuguese forced Ullal to give as a symbol of accepting their colonial authority.\nQuestion 2. Complete the sentence with a suitable reason.\nRani Abbakka says, \u201cWe are a sovereign country\u201d because _____________.\nAnswer:\nShe wanted to prove that Ullal was independent and did not have to follow or pay tribute to the Portuguese rulers.\nQuestion 3. Identify whether the following statement is true or false.\nThe Portuguese envoy threatened Rani Abbakka.\nAnswer:\nTrue\nQuestion 4. Choose a word given in brackets to replace the underlined word.\n\u201c\u2026 she defied the Portuguese and established a hugely profitable trading relation with Arabia.\u201d (defeated/disobeyed)\nAnswer:\ndisobeyed.\nQuestion 5. Choose the option that lists the qualities of Rani Abbakka, based on this extract.\n(i) bold\n(ii) thoughtful\n(iii) capable\n(iv) generous\n(v) determined\nA. (i), (ii), and (v)\nB. (ii), (iii), and (iv)\nC. (i), (iii), and (v)\nD. (ii), (iv), and (v)\nAnswer:\nOption C (i), (iii), and (v)- bold, capable and determined.\nII. Answer the following questions.\nQuestion 1. Rani Abbakka spoke to her mother on her deathbed. How might these words have made her mother feel?\nAnswer:\nRani Abbakka\u2019s words to her mother in her final moments would have filled her mother with pride, reassurance, and hope, knowing that her daughter was determined to defend their kingdom with courage.\nQuestion 2. What does the support of the people of Ullal and the soldiers for Rani Abbakka suggest about their mindset?\nAnswer:\nThe citizens of Ullal, along with its soldiers, displayed immense courage, loyalty, and pride in their land. They were prepared to safeguard Ullal\u2019s independence no matter the sacrifice. Their unity reflected their deep faith in Rani Abbakka and their firm determination to oppose Portuguese domination.\nQuestion 3. How might the people of Ullal have felt when the mighty Portuguese were defeated?\nAnswer:\nThe people of Ullal would have been filled with happiness and pride after overcoming the powerful Portuguese forces. They likely rejoiced in their regained freedom and deeply appreciated the courage shown by Rani Abbakka.\nQuestion 4. Why do you think Rani Abbakka\u2019s victory against the Portuguese would have inspired other rulers to go against a foreign power?\nAnswer:\nRani Abbakka\u2019s triumph proved that a strong and dominant foreign power could be overcome through bravery and collective strength. Her success would have motivated other rulers to rise against outside domination and defend their independence.\nRani Abbakka Class 7 Questions and Answers \u2013 Let us learn (Pages 215-220)\nI. Study the following words taken from the text.\nseize, sovereign, their, soldiers\nThe spelling of the given words have \u2018ei\u2019 and \u2018ie\u2019 in them.\nSpelling tip: \u2018i\u2019 before \u2018e\u2019 except after \u2018c\u2019\nFor example: receive, deceive\nNow, fill in the blanks with \u2018ie\u2019 or \u2018ei\u2019 for the following words."
