      "q": "1. India\u2019s past was heroic, and at present, the pace of her development is inspiring. Women play a significant role in it. These women are around us, inspiring tts all the time.\nWith these thoughts, write a conversation between two students, Pratap and Tarana, discussing the role played by women in forming India\u2019s identity as a strong nation.\nYou may begin like this:\nPratap: Tarana, I have a lot of respect for women like\u2026\nTarana: I believe in the capabilities of women. Did you \u2026?\nComplete the conversation in about six to eight sentences for each of them and share your answers with your classmates and the teacher.",
      "a": "wer:\nPratap: Tarana, I truly admire remarkable women like Rani Lakshmibai, Sarojini Naidu, and Kalpana Chawla. Each of them made outstanding contributions in their own fields.\nTarana: I have great faith in women\u2019s abilities. You know, women played an important part in India\u2019s freedom movement and continue to help shape the nation even today.\nPratap: Absolutely! Besides the freedom fighters, leaders like Indira Gandhi and Kiran Bedi have been influential figures in politics and administration.\nTarana: Right! Today, women are achieving excellence in science, sports, entrepreneurship, and even space missions. Take Mary Kom, for example\u2014she has brought immense pride to India through boxing.\nPratap: And we must also acknowledge women like Dr. Tessy Thomas, known as the \u201cMissile Woman of India,\u201d who has made significant contributions to the country\u2019s defence research.\nTarana: Exactly! Women are demonstrating that they are capable of matching men in every field. Their determination and bravery are helping India progress every day.\nPratap: It is our responsibility to support them so they can continue breaking obstacles and inspiring future generations.\nTarana: Absolutely! A country becomes truly strong only when both men and women move forward together with equal respect and opportunity.\nClass 7th English Chapter 15 Rani Abbakka Question Answer \u2013 Let us explore (Page 222)\nQuestion 1. In groups of five, find facts about any one brave woman who we remember because of her achievements and present in class. For example, Rani Chennamma of Kittur, Rani Durgavati, Ahilyabai Holkar, Jhalkari Bai, Captain Lakshmi Sahgal, Kanaklata Barua, Kalpana Chawla, or anyone else.\nInclude the following in your presentation:"
